    ],
    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Ramón Salvador Águeda is a Spanish property developer associated with Elche and the wider Alicante and Murcia markets. He led Grupo RS and was the principal shareholder of Residencial Mira Llevant, pursuing land transactions and housing developments. He also represented his local industry as president of the Elche builders' association.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When Ramón Salvador took his property business into southern Brazil, he chose to begin with homes that were simpler to build. Grupo RS bought land around Porto Alegre and planned to reach lower-income buyers after adapting its construction methods. Its designs included lifts and accessible apartments, linking the proposed expansion to the practical requirements of a different housing market.\n\nHis Spanish career also became entangled in urban-planning litigation. He was among the defendants tried over Alicante's proposed development plan in the Brugal case. The Alicante provincial court acquitted him in 2021, while two other defendants received fines for bribery.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 86,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full contemporaneous Brazil report supports plans and construction rationale, without asserting completed output. Full RTVE court report establishes his acquittal in the specific proceeding."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S5",
      "S6"
    ],
    "word_count": 99,
    "html": "<p>When Ramón Salvador took his property business into southern Brazil, he chose to begin with homes that were simpler to build. Grupo RS bought land around Porto Alegre and planned to reach lower-income buyers after adapting its construction methods. Its designs included lifts and accessible apartments, linking the proposed expansion to the practical requirements of a different housing market.</p>\r\n<p>His Spanish career also became entangled in urban-planning litigation. He was among the defendants tried over Alicante's proposed development plan in the Brugal case. The Alicante provincial court acquitted him in 2021, while two other defendants received fines for bribery.</p>\r\n"
  },
